Subject: [PATCH 10986/11362] Sixth doc/YAML point holds the split; the floor
 lint's first true positive

Milestone 610 declares 14 tasks and queued 7. That makes three clean at 12 and
three divergent at 14 across six milestones with no counterexample, and 610's 7
matches what 607 produced from the same 14-task document.

Counted from the document's own stated task count rather than by grepping
experiment ids, per the method correction I had to make yesterday when that grep
over-counted 609 by three and nearly produced a false divergence. Still no
13-task plan in the record, so the boundary stays bracketed between 12 and 14.

Records separately that the word-boundary floor lint reported its first non-zero
since the fix, and that it is genuine: exp6968-arc-post-refit-induction-audit,
scoped by the bare word arc, naming arc_e3_induced_model_quality and
arc_executable_world_model, signalling on held-out and generalization. The fix
therefore does both halves of its job in production -- it stopped matching on
research and still catches a real ARC task. Worth stating because a fix that
only removes false positives looks identical to one that removes everything
until a true positive appears.

Also notes for whoever continues the induce work that exp6968 is the held-out
scoring half of the measurement this session is running the generation half of,
so the two are complementary rather than duplicated effort.

